{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long double ld;\n\nvoid dfs(int pos, int n, int mask, int cnt, ld s, const ld p[], ld sum[], int sz[]) {\n    if (pos == n) {\n        sz[mask] = cnt;\n        sum[mask] = s;\n        return;\n    }\n\n    dfs(pos + 1, n, mask, cnt, s, p, sum, sz);\n    dfs(pos + 1, n, mask | (1 << pos), cnt + 1, s + p[pos], p, sum, sz);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n, k;\n    scanf(\"%d%d\", &n, &k);\n\n    static ld p[20];\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        double x;\n        scanf(\"%lf\", &x);\n        p[i] = x;\n    }\n\n    static ld c[21][21], coef[21], sum[1 << 20];\n    static int sz[1 << 20];\n\n    c[0][0] = 1.0L;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        c[i][0] = 1.0L;\n        for (int j = 1; j <= i; ++j)\n            c[i][j] = c[i - 1][j - 1] + c[i - 1][j];\n    }\n\n    dfs(0, n, 0, 0, 0.0L, p, sum, sz);\n\n    for (int i = k - 1; i >= 0; --i) {\n        coef[i] = 1.0L - coef[i];\n        for (int j = 1; i - j >= 0; ++j)\n            coef[i - j] += c[n - 1 - i + j][j] * coef[i];\n    }\n\n    int lim = 1 << n;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        ld ans = 0.0L;\n        if (p[i] > 0.005) {\n            for (int mask = 0; mask < lim; ++mask) {\n                if ((mask >> i) & 1) continue;\n                if (sz[mask] >= k) continue;\n                ans += coef[sz[mask]] / (1.0L - sum[mask]);\n            }\n        }\n        printf(\"%.12lf \", (double)(p[i] * ans));\n    }\n\n    printf(\"\\n\");\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 1.0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef solve() -> None:\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    it = iter(data)\n    n = int(next(it))\n    k = int(next(it))\n    p = [float(next(it)) for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # binomial coefficients C[n][k]\n    C = [[0.0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    C[0][0] = 1.0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        C[i][0] = 1.0\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            C[i][j] = C[i - 1][j - 1] + C[i - 1][j]\n\n    lim = 1 << n\n    sum_ = [0.0] * lim\n    sz = [0] * lim\n\n    # depth-first search to fill sum_ and sz for all masks\n    def dfs(pos: int, mask: int, cnt: int, s: float) -> None:\n        if pos == n:\n            sz[mask] = cnt\n            sum_[mask] = s\n            return\n        # do not take element pos\n        dfs(pos + 1, mask, cnt, s)\n        # take element pos\n        dfs(pos + 1, mask | (1 << pos), cnt + 1, s + p[pos])\n\n    dfs(0, 0, 0, 0.0)\n\n    # coef array of size k (only indices 0..k-1 used)\n    coef = [0.0] * k\n    for i in range(k - 1, -1, -1):\n        coef[i] = 1.0 - coef[i]\n        # j from 1 while i-j >= 0\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            coef[i - j] += C[n - 1 - i + j][j] * coef[i]\n\n    out = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        ans = 0.0\n        if p[i] > 0.005:\n            for mask in range(lim):\n                if (mask >> i) & 1:\n                    continue\n                if sz[mask] >= k:\n                    continue\n                ans += coef[sz[mask]] / (1.0 - sum_[mask])\n        out.append(\"{:.12f}\".format(p[i] * ans))\n    sys.stdout.write(\" \".join(out) + \"\\n\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.6027750372886658, -0.0489935502409935, -2.9682672902708873e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -0.00044526674901135266, -0.0011975744273513556, -2.1457441107486375e-05, -0.023280154913663864, -3.099393507000059e-05, -0.6240565180778503, -0.25194740295410156, -5.364403477869928e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -0.007855593226850033, -5.173549288883805e-05, -0.0005198557628318667, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -0.00034767304896377027, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.014165564440190792, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -3.814689989667386e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -7.652943895664066e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -0.00012337400403339416, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.7417760065873154e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00582343153655529, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -5.483612312673358e-06, -9.298280929215252e-06, -4.768360213347478e-06, -6.794906312279636e-06, -2.4676019165781327e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -4.95898348162882e-05, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.2914423829643056e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -0.1269320398569107, -0.07889272272586823, -0.002521432936191559, -3.075552376685664e-05, -0.011051633395254612, -0.9741423726081848, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -9.059865078597795e-06, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.03819403424859047, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.0005907459417358041, -0.24713587760925293, -0.00016246906307060272, -0.9515689611434937, -0.7810959815979004, -0.062180254608392715, -1.067715048789978, -0.3944410383701324